{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01BbmMp1Sb4MRtdjjqQm2w65","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Selection goldens (Epic 03 Story 2, G1–G4)\n2\t\n3\tCommitted expected arrangements for the band-selection walk (tech design\n4\t§Deterministic Algorithms), consumed by `test/view-select-golden.test.ts`.\n5\tEach golden pins the exact arrangement a compact must produce on the Story-0\n6\tfixture (or its straggler variant) under explicit params: subject ids per\n7\tband, form used, compact point, covered_from, and gaps.\n8\t\n9\t**Goldens are immutable once committed.** An implementation that disagrees\n10\twith a golden is wrong until the *design rule* is shown wrong — that takes the\n11\tdeviation process, not a golden edit. The expected values were hand-derived\n12\tfrom the design's rules (rules 1–6, the pinned ≤/newest-first/newest-member\n13\ttie-breakers) against the fixture's deterministic token costs.\n14\t\n15\tRegenerated once under impl-lead ruling\n16\t`02-smart-compact-story-run-001-ruling-013`: the first commit's goldens\n17\tencoded extra-rule selection behavior (smooth-obligate inclusion,\n18\tpartial-chunk retreat, suppressed brief loner); these goldens encode the\n19\tliteral rules.\n20\t\n21\t| File | Case | Rule under test |\n22\t|------|------|-----------------|\n23\t| `g1-proportions.json` | G1 | shares → bands across the full gradient |\n24\t| `g2-edge-inclusion.json` | G2a | entry exactly filling the remainder is included (≤) |\n25\t| `g2-edge-exclusion.json` | G2b | one token under the exact fill → excluded, band stops |\n26\t| `g3-oversized-loner.json` | G3 | oversized entry on an otherwise-empty band represents alone |\n27\t| `g4-turnless-straggler.json` | G4 | rule 6: straggler rides the following turn's band entry; trailing straggler is tail |\n28\t\n29\t## Regeneration (only with a granted deviation)\n30\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a19a2d2c-079f-4c8b-a6d9-08d7c8df8763","uuid":"e1841123-3350-47a4-aa23-05e64923bcd0","timestamp":"2026-06-11T17:42:30.408Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/test/goldens/README.md","content":"# Selection goldens (Epic 03 Story 2, G1–G4)\n\nCommitted expected arrangements for the band-selection walk (tech design\n§Deterministic Algorithms), consumed by `test/view-select-golden.test.ts`.\nEach golden pins the exact arrangement a compact must produce on the Story-0\nfixture (or its straggler variant) under explicit params: subject ids per\nband, form used, compact point, covered_from, and gaps.\n\n**Goldens are immutable once committed.** An implementation that disagrees\nwith a golden is wrong until the *design rule* is shown wrong — that takes the\ndeviation process, not a golden edit. The expected values were hand-derived\nfrom the design's rules (rules 1–6, the pinned ≤/newest-first/newest-member\ntie-breakers) against the fixture's deterministic token costs.\n\nRegenerated once under impl-lead ruling\n`02-smart-compact-story-run-001-ruling-013`: the first commit's goldens\nencoded extra-rule selection behavior (smooth-obligate inclusion,\npartial-chunk retreat, suppressed brief loner); these goldens encode the\nliteral rules.\n\n| File | Case | Rule under test |\n|------|------|-----------------|\n| `g1-proportions.json` | G1 | shares → bands across the full gradient |\n| `g2-edge-inclusion.json` | G2a | entry exactly filling the remainder is included (≤) |\n| `g2-edge-exclusion.json` | G2b | one token under the exact fill → excluded, band stops |\n| `g3-oversized-loner.json` | G3 | oversized entry on an otherwise-empty band represents alone |\n| `g4-turnless-straggler.json` | G4 | rule 6: straggler rides the following turn's band entry; trailing straggler is tail |\n\n## Regeneration (only with a granted deviation)\n","numLines":30,"startLine":1,"totalLines":41}}}
